<p>Find the order of each DE.</p>

<p>
  1. <m>y''' + x^8 y'' + y' = 0</m>
  <answer name="part1">
    <shortDescription>y''' + x^8 y'' + y' = 0</shortDescription> 3
  </answer>
</p>
<feedback condition="$part1=8">
  Recall that
  <me>x^8 = x\cdot x \cdot x\cdot x\cdot x\cdot x\cdot x\cdot x,</me> represents
  multiplication of <m>x</m>, not its derivative.
</feedback>
<p>
  2. <m>\displaystyle \frac{d^2y}{dx^2}+7y \left(\frac{dy}{dx}\right)^5 = 8</m>
  <answer name="de2">
    <shortDescription>(d^2y)/(dx^2) + 7y (dy/dx)^5=8</shortDescription> 2
  </answer>
</p>
<feedback condition="$de2=5">
  Careful, <me>\left(\frac{dy}{dx}\right)^5</me> is not the fifth derivative. It
  is the first derivative to the 5th power!
</feedback>
<p>
  3. <m>\displaystyle\frac{du}{dt} = y^2 +\sin(u)</m>
  <answer><shortDescription>du/dt = y^2 + sin(u)</shortDescription> 1</answer>
</p>
<p>
  4. <m>\displaystyle y^{(5)}(x) = e^{y(x)}+y'(x)</m>
  <answer>
    <shortDescription>y^{(5)}(x) = e^{y(x)}+y'(x)</shortDescription> 5
  </answer>
</p>
<p>
  5. <m>\displaystyle \frac{d^2y}{dt^2} - \frac{d^2y}{dx^2}+\sin(y)=0</m>
  <answer>
    <shortDescription>(d^2y)/(dt^2) - (d^2y)(dx^2)+sin(y)=0</shortDescription> 2
  </answer>
</p>
<p>
  6. <m>\ddddot{y} + 2x\dot{y} + y = 0</m>
  <answer name="part6">
    <shortDescription><m>\ddot{y} + 2x\dot{y} + y = 0</m></shortDescription> 4
  </answer>
</p>
<feedback condition="$part6.creditAchieved">
  The "dot" notation dates back to Newton's original work on derivatives. It is
  still used widely in physics to denote a derivative with respect to time, and
  then mixed with the prime notation for derivatives with respect to space.
</feedback>